# Round 11 Review — the prepare-branch verification pass

**Scope:** iteration 2 of the review-fix loop over the same wave
(`807afc9..0aca877` plus round 10's fixes), run at the owner's request
via the prepare-branch skill's loop adapted to main (the skill refuses
main and requires a PR; the loop ran, the GitHub handoff did not — no
PR exists). Five lenses re-reviewed the full surface with the round-10
fix diff included. **The pass found 13 new actionable defects —
including one in round 10's own fix — all fixed in this commit.**

## Blocking (fixed)

| ID | Finding | Fix |
|----|---------|-----|
| R11-1 | **Round 10's batch-id fix was half-applied**: the wire trait impl stubbed `to_memory_id` to `""`, so the ONLINE submit path (MCP `end_session` and CLI `add`) still hashed without the cross-batch target — the exact defect R10-6 set out to close; the parity test only exercised empty targets. | The wire impl returns its real field; new test pins differing-target -> differing-id. |
| R11-2 | **GitHub windows split PRs from their closing-reference rows**: chunking walked raw rows with no affinity, so an edge's endpoints could land in different windows — the SDK rejects the unit (`InvalidUnit`) and a resubmit dies at the same straddle forever. | The chunker groups each PR atomically with its closing refs (lib-level `chunk_windows`, `Window` type); tests pin affinity. |
| R11-3 | The `known` set was never updated when appending closing refs — a doubly-closed issue produced duplicate draft keys in one unit (`InvalidUnit`). | Dedupe moved into the chunker (carried refs never also stand alone); test pins single-row. |
| R11-4 | **Per-window cursors could regress mid-run** (closing refs appended unsorted; per-chunk max dipped; the unconditional write persisted the regression). | Groups emit oldest-first by their NEWEST row; chunk cursors monotonic by construction; test pins it. |
| R11-5 | Cursor writes were plain `fs::write` — a torn write truncates the resume point (the SDK itself uses tmp+rename). | `save_cursor_atomic` (tmp+rename) in all three adapter mains. |
| R11-6 | **git `--range` one-shot clobbered the sequential cursor**: writing the range's HEAD strands the gap before it; the next run sees `HEAD..HEAD` and the gap is never ingested. | The operator cursor advances only in sequential mode. |
| R11-7 | git's cursor read swallowed all errors (the sibling adapters' NotFound-vs-fatal pattern existed; git lacked it). | Same fail-closed read as linear/github. |

## Advisory (fixed)

- **R11-8** README's operator docs omitted kind 7 from the policy list;
  MILESTONE said 1-5. Both corrected (an admin following the old README
  would re-introduce R10-7's mislabeled-provenance workaround).
- **R11-9** No regression net for the policy-kind table (R10-7) or the
  operator-cursor writes (R10-1). Added: kinds 6/7 + 8-fails-closed in
  the server's policy test; a REAL-BINARY git test asserting the
  operator cursor file is written after a settled window.
- **R11-10** `--draft` had zero coverage. cli_smoke now writes a draft
  file with its own `draft_key`, links via `--link`, and asserts the
  edge landed — the exact R10-5 regression shape.
- **R11-11** GitHub's chunker was main-private and untested. Now
  lib-level with four tests (affinity, monotonic cursors, oversize
  bail, no-duplicate rows).
- **R11-12** The rate-limit test asserted only `is_some()`; now pins
  the variant and both payload fields. Plus cleanup: `title` expect
  over silent-default, api-client stale header ("GitHub's next") and
  double no-retries claim, `panic_reason` helper dedupe, github header
  line contradicting R10-2, tautological `has_next ||` assert, comment
  trims.
- **R11-13** Adapters exited 0 with permanently-rejected rows behind
  the advanced cursor (silent terminal loss to a scheduler). All three
  now finish the run, then exit 2 with a named count.

## Recorded (not fixed)

- Linear/GitHub binary-level cursor-write tests (the mock-server spawn
  pattern is proven by git's new test; the two mains need the same
  harness) — follow-up with the R10-18 adapter-runner extraction.
- The lib-level helper twins (`parse_visibility` etc.) join the
  R10-18 duplication record.

## Carried unverified (dispositions)

Retired: epoch-0 `observed_at` (the live GitHub leg committed with
it); server-side duplicate-edge dedup (moot — deduped client-side).
Carried: GitHub `filterBy.since` inclusivity, `gte: null` acceptance,
tonic over https backends, hyper error Display embedding URIs — all
external-API behaviors needing a live leg to adjudicate.

## The verification pass (iteration 3) — 8 more, all fixed

A full-charter pass over the round-11 diff found the loop had not yet
converged; all eight are fixed in the same commit as this addendum:

- **R11V-1 (blocking)** Two PRs closing the SAME issue put one row
  twice into a shared window (duplicate draft_key -> SDK `InvalidUnit`
  -> permanent livelock). Windows now dedupe rows within themselves;
  a row repeated ACROSS windows is legal and replays idempotently.
  Test pins the shared-window case.
- **R11V-2** git lacked the exit-2-on-permanent-rejections path its
  siblings gained (R11-13).
- **R11V-3** git's three round-11 fixes had no net: added a REAL-BINARY
  test that a `--range` one-shot run leaves the sequential cursor
  untouched (and dropped a dead mock script entry).
- **R11V-4** The monotonicity test could not fail without the sort
  (inputs were pre-sorted). New test feeds pulls newest-first with a
  closing ref NEWER than its PR and an interleaved standalone issue.
- **R11V-5** The `--draft` contract's other clauses (title optional;
  disagreeing type rejected by name) now pinned in cli_smoke.
- **R11V-6** Two vacuous asserts (`let _ = rel("")`, `let _ = draft_id`)
  and an unreachable `unwrap_or_default` removed.
- **R11V-7** Three operator-facing bail strings carried rewrap
  artifacts (long space runs) — rewritten as single lines.
- **R11V-8 (pre-existing, same class)** git's windows bounded COMMITS,
  not memory rows (commits + their file rows); a busy window exceeded
  the declared bound exactly as github's did before R11-3. Windows now
  count commits plus the distinct paths they introduce.

Loop status after this fix: iterations 1-4 complete; a further full
pass is required before claiming a clean exit.
